== Lesson Two<answers2>
5. #set enum(spacing: 1.5em)
  + Where do we two live?
  + You are and we two are.
  + I live and those two remember.
  + You two ask and he remembers.
  + Where are we two going?
  + Where am I?
  + Where am I going (or) Where do I go?
  + I ask and he remembers.
  + You live and we two go.
  + Where are you going? (or) Where do you go?
+ Use only one verb. The auxiliary verb "are" need not be
  translated when there is another verb.

  (Just observe the sentences in parentheses, written with the #sandhi
  included.)

  + #romanization[kutra gacchathaḥ] \
      (#romanization[kutra gacchathaḥ])
  + #romanization[vasāmi ca vasataḥ ca] \
      (#romanization[vasāmi ca vasataś ca])
