\
+ There is a crocodile in the Ganges.
+ A monkey lives on the bank (of the river).
+ The monkey throws down fruit for the crocodile.
+ The crocodile eats the fruit.
+ The wife wants (to eat) the monkey’s heart.
+ "The heart is in the tree!", the monkey says.
+ "Someone steals the heart", the monkey says.
+ Therefore, the crocodile and the monkey remain friends (stand
  in friendship).

